We will begin with the Framing phase, paying close attention to confidentiality, existing production tools, and seasonality of workload, as is our standard practice for professional services clients. This phase will be crucial in ensuring that we understand Cabinet Vauclair Associés' specific needs and constraints, including their budgetary limitations and operating cost control requirements.

Our dedicated team, consisting of a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, will work closely with the client to ensure that our flagship product, Atelier, is tailored to meet their requirements. We will also leverage our partnerships with OuraneCloud for hosting and Ligeo Conseil for integration with Cabinet Vauclair Associés' existing production tools.

To maintain decision traceability, we will establish a joint steering committee with the client, which will meet monthly, and an operational committee that meets fortnightly. Roles will be formalized in a RACI matrix, ensuring clear accountability and communication channels. Our single accountable project director will serve as the primary point of contact for the client.

By following our established governance practices and leveraging our past experiences, we can ensure that the project is delivered within the allocated budget of 220,000 over 3 years while controlling annual operating costs. The phased approach with a pilot phase followed by progressive rollout will allow us to demonstrate the value of our solution, Atelier, while minimizing risks and ensuring decision traceability throughout the project lifecycle.
